.TH FASTENT 1 "2026-05-20" "fastent 1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fastent \- entropy and randomness tester
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastent
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B fastent
.B \-r
.RI [ options ]
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastent
measures entropy and statistical randomness in a byte or bit stream. With no
path, it reads standard input. Normal output contains Shannon entropy,
chi-square and its upper-tail probability, arithmetic mean, a Monte Carlo
estimate of pi, and serial correlation.
.PP
The program dispatches SIMD kernels at run time and can split work across
threads. Results are stable across supported kernels, I/O modes, and thread
counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bits
Treat the input as bits. Histograms have two bins and the mean is relative to
0.5. The Monte Carlo test remains byte based.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-counts
Include an occurrence table.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fold
Fold ASCII and Latin-1 uppercase letters before analysis.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-terse
Write CSV.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-json
Write JSON. This takes precedence over CSV and annotated output.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extended
Add min-entropy, collision entropy, index of coincidence, poker, variance,
standard deviation, redundancy, symbol summaries, bit-position bias, LZ77F,
and Bandt-Pompe permutation entropy.
.IP
Repeat the option. The
.B \-ee
level adds order-1 conditional entropy, adjacent mutual information, runs,
longest run, and bit cusum. The
.B \-eee
level adds 512-bit Berlekamp-Massey complexity, Maurer universal, and NIST
32x32 binary matrix-rank tests.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-annotate
Write a PASS, WEAK, or FAIL report with short explanations. Implies
.BR \-e .
It cannot be combined with recursive mode.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-full-precision
Print floating-point values with enough digits to round-trip binary64.
.TP
.BR \-j " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-threads= \fIN\fR
Use
.I N
workers. The value
.B auto
uses the online CPU count. This option is absent from builds without a thread
backend.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " "\-\-io=" \fIMODE\fR
Select input handling.
.B auto
maps regular files and streams other inputs;
.B mmap
requires a mapping;
.B stream
uses ordinary reads; and
.B uring
uses io_uring on Linux or IOCP on Windows. An unavailable explicitly selected
backend is an error.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-histogram
Draw the selected distribution. Active extended tests add their own plots.
Terminals use block glyphs; redirected output uses ASCII.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log
Use a logarithmic Y axis for histograms.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " "\-\-color=" \fIMODE\fR
Set color to
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Walk a directory and write one CSV row per regular file, or a JSON array with
.BR \-J .
.TP
.BI \-\-sort-by= COL [: asc |: desc ]
Sort recursive output. Basic columns are
.BR path ,
.BR samples ,
.BR entropy ,
.BR chisq ,
.BR mean ,
.BR pi ,
and
.BR scc .
Extended columns use the field names printed by CSV. Their selection enables
the needed extended level. Numeric columns default to descending order; paths
default to ascending order.
.TP
.B \-\-fips\-140\-2
Run the FIPS 140-2 monobit, poker, runs, and long-run power-up tests over each
complete 20,000-bit block. Normal analysis is skipped. Recursive mode is not
supported.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and license notice.
.SH OUTPUT
Plain output describes one stream. CSV and JSON retain stable field names for
scripts. Values that cannot be computed are written as
.BR nan
or JSON
.BR null .
.PP
Annotated output gives each applicable metric a verdict. PASS is below two
standard deviations, WEAK is below three, and FAIL is at least three where a
normal score exists. Advisory statistics are marked separately. These screens
do not certify a random generator.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Analysis completed, or every FIPS block passed.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, failed FIPS block, or refused option combination.
.TP
.B 2
I/O, allocation, or platform error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fastent sample.bin
fastent -a -ee sample.bin
fastent -b -H random.bin
generator | fastent -J
fastent -r --sort-by=entropy data/
fastent --fips-140-2 rng.bin
.fi
.SH PERFORMANCE
The order-0 path uses banked SIMD histograms. Mapped files are split into
aligned slabs; streams use a bounded shared pipeline. The extended grid tests
process fixed 4 MiB blocks. Higher
.B \-e
levels cost more, with Berlekamp-Massey normally the slowest test.
.SH PORTABILITY
The C99 sources support common Linux, Windows, macOS, OpenBSD, and FreeBSD
hosts. Release builds also cover WebAssembly, Windows 95, DJGPP/MS-DOS, and
several further Linux architectures.
.PP
The runtime may dispatch scalar, SSSE3, SSE4.1, AVX2, AVX-512, NEON, SVE2, or
WebAssembly SIMD128 kernels when they were built and the host supports them.
.SH LIMITS
Several tests need large samples. Underpowered tests return no verdict. LZ77F
and permutation entropy restart at 4 MiB boundaries and therefore have a small,
bounded difference from whole-stream forms. FIPS mode ignores a final partial
20,000-bit block.
.SH AUTHOR
Kamila Szewczyk <k@iczelia.net>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ent (1),
.BR rngtest (1),
.BR dieharder (1),
.BR od (1)
